> Included Utility Scripts

SNAPS-OS has a couple of utility scripts, all of which can be found under ~/.config/snapsos

#help/cmd-help.sh#
this script presents a searchable list of commands with their TLDR explainers on the right.
the list of commands can be found in cmds.list.
when the user selects a command, it'll open the man page for that command.

this is bound to *super+H* and the terminal alias `tldrtui`

#help/help.sh#
shows this menu! it effectively shows you all the files in the topics folder with their contents.

this is bound to *super+shift+H* and the terminal alias `helptui`

#help/references.sh#
this script takes a list file (like references.list, mangoipc.list or DMSipc.list) and presents it using fzf.
this is used by the documentation TUI to present searchable reference lists.

#screenshots/mode-toggle.sh#
this script rotates between 3 save modes for screenshots. modes are:
save to clipboard / save to file / open in editor

this is bound to *PrintScreen*

#screenshots/fullscreen.sh#
takes an all-screen screenshot

this is bound to *super+ctrl+PrintScreen*

#screenshots/region.sh#
allows you to select a region to capture

this is bound to *super+PrintScreen*

#tips/tips.list#
source file the tips system pulls from. the line that fetches tips:
`shuf -n 1 ~/.config/snapsos/tips/tips.list`

this runs automatically on opening your first terminal (not on successive terminals)
you can also get a tip by running `tipme` in the terminal or pressing *super+0*

#tuis/aur-install.sh#
provides a graphical interface for browsing the AUR, including multi-select and a details pane

launch with the terminal alias `aurgui`

#tuis/pkg-install.sh#
provides a graphical interface for browsing the pacman repository, including multi-select and a details pane

launch with the terminal alias `pacgui`

#tuis/documentation.sh#
provides quick access to various pieces of documentation and interactive reference lists

launch with the alias `documentation` or the bind *super+shift+M*

#tuis/layout-switch.sh#
allows you to switch layouts using a selectable menu, pulls layouts from layouts.list

launch with the bind *super+shift+W*

#tuis/project-select.sh#
shows a list of git repositories within your projects directory (default ~/projects) with their top-level files and readme.
when you select a repo, it opens in code-oss (vscode).

launch with the alias `git-projects` or the bind *super+shift+tab*

#tuis/bar-presets.sh#
presents an FZF menu to toggle pre-configured bars and dock, as well as select from combination presets.

launch with *super+shift+D*

#mango-config.sh#
gives a browsable TUI for all config files in ~/.config/mango with a preview; selecting opens in micro.

launch with the alias `mangoconf` or the bind *super+M*

#config-overview/menu.sh#
gives a browsable TUI that shows details for each line in your mango config file.

launch with *super+alt+M*

#wallpapers/setwallpapergroup.sh#
called with a folder name or without. with a folder name, sets wallpapers to that folder.
without, presents a menu to select a folder.

bound to *super+W*, cycling forward/back with *alt+W* and *shift+alt+W*

#optional: unipkg#
opened via `unipkg launch-tui`, `unipkg help-tui` or `unipkg help`
also bound to *super+shift+Y*

#optional: dotfile-git-sync#
run from the terminal: `dotfile-git-sync ~/path/to/your/github/repository`
shows a menu to multi-select folders from ~/.config, moves them to your repo, symlinks with stow, and syncs to github.
